<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="007" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Schema: v4 data needs and the episode-scoped dedupe key</title>
    <phase>0 Foundations</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Dataverse column adds on five ontology tables; logical names are immutable, so a wrong name is delete-and-recreate after code is written against it.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Repeats task 001's recorded Web API recipe; every column is named below.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>008, 009, 036 and 037 all read the columns this task creates.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>001</deps>
    <tags>dataverse,schema,signals,decision-record</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add the columns the owner's 2026-10-07 decisions require on sprk_signal, sprk_policy, sprk_policyversion and sprk_decisionrecord, and make sprk_dedupekey able to carry the episode suffix, using the Web API recipe task 001 used.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Schema first, verified by query, before any code is written against it.</role>
  <goal>Every column listed under Steps exists in OntologyPlatformSolution under prefix sprk, verified by a live describe; sprk_dedupekey holds the longest episode-scoped key; the existing dev Signals carry an episode-1 key.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Owner decisions 2026-10-07 (spec section 9): D-13 makes the dedupe key episode-scoped ({policycode}|{type}|{id}|{episode}) so a resolved Signal can re-raise, and the Do lane re-raises only when the subject's date changed since resolution, which needs the date the Signal last saw (sprk_signal.sprk_duedate). D-17 makes the one Decision Record list the actual outcome of every action (sprk_steps) and the Next steps created (sprk_followons). D-16/D-18/D-19 give a rule several actions, so the version needs a decision plan (sprk_decisionplan) instead of the single sprk_proposedaction text. D-22 slice (a) needs Retire with a reason. D-23 composes the row headline from the Signal's display columns, including the rule's short name. Reconciliation rows S-2, S-5, S-6, S-10 and v4-prototype-vs-solution entries #1, #2, #6, #7 carry the evidence.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/schema-draft.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/001-schema-verification.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/v4-reconciliation.md</file>
      <file role="modify">projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/schema-draft.md</file>
      <file role="new">projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/007-schema-verification.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: every column in this task is created via the recorded Web API recipe (notes/schema-draft.md banner): explicit PascalCase SchemaName, the MSCRM.SolutionUniqueName header for OntologyPlatformSolution, DateTimeBehavior on every date column. NEVER MCP create_table or any tool without a publisher parameter (this environment's default publisher is new and logical names are immutable).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: create exactly these columns and no others. sprk_signal: sprk_duedate (Date Only, behaviour DateOnly; the subject's due or response date, refreshed while the Signal is open). sprk_policy: sprk_severity (choice, D-30, see the next constraint), sprk_shortname (text, 100), sprk_worktype (choice; values = the v4 work types per lane listed in notes/v4-reconciliation.md W-8: Ask outside counsel, Approve or rebudget, Chase a reply, Finish or reschedule, Coming due, Chase a response), sprk_retiredreason (multiline text) plus a statuscode value Retired on the Inactive state. sprk_policyversion: sprk_decisionplan (multiline text, JSON). sprk_signal and sprk_decisionrecord: sprk_project (lookup to sprk_project, optional; D-34, see the constraints below). sprk_decisionrecord: sprk_steps (multiline text, JSON), sprk_followons (multiline text, JSON), sprk_gatetier (text, 100).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: sprk_dedupekey is NOT recreated. Read its current MaxLength; if the longest key ({policycode max 100}|{type}|{36-char guid}|{episode up to 6 digits}) does not fit, raise MaxLength on the existing column (an in-place metadata update; record before and after). The alternate key on sprk_dedupekey must stay Active.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: re-key every existing sprk_signal row (dev seed only) by appending |1 to its sprk_dedupekey (D-13: existing Signals are episode 1). Record the row count before and after; zero rows is a valid result and must be recorded as such.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">AMENDED 2026-10-07 (D-30): add sprk_policy.sprk_severity, a choice column reusing sprk_signal.sprk_severity's values (Info 100000000, Warning 100000001, Critical 100000002; read the live option set and reuse a global option set if the Signal's is global), optional, no default. The UI labels High / Medium / Low are display only (Critical = High, Warning = Medium, Info = Low); the admin sets it per rule.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">AMENDED 2026-10-07 (D-34): add a typed sprk_project lookup (to sprk_project, optional) on sprk_signal and on sprk_decisionrecord, beside the existing typed sprk_matter: the item's core record is whichever ONE of the two is set. SHAPE CHOSEN and why: typed lookups per core entity, with NO separate core-record type column and NO polymorphic choice. That is how uac-r2 models core records: the FR-26 stamps are one typed lookup per CORE entity (CoreAncestorResolver.CoreAncestorLookups), and the intermediates that name their root directly use typed sprk_matter / sprk_project pairs (sprk_invoice, sprk_budget, sprk_document in IntermediateRootColumns; sprk_invoice carries both, live read 2026-10-07). The sprk_regardingproject column already on sprk_signal is NOT reused: on the Signal the sprk_regarding* lookups are the ADR-024 SUBJECT, not the grouping record (task 030). No column is added for work assignment or service request (O-22).</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">AMENDED 2026-10-07 (D-35, replaces the D-31 constraint): an item with no matter and no project gets a Signal (and later a Decision Record) with both core-record columns null; the core-record columns are optional for this case only. Read the RequiredLevel of sprk_signal.sprk_matter and sprk_decisionrecord.sprk_matter; if either is ApplicationRequired, set it to None (D-35 decides this) and record before and after; the "only for this case" rule is enforced by the writers (037, 040), not by the platform.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: do NOT add a separate sprk_episode column. The episode lives in the key (D-13); the writer finds the latest episode by a begins-with query on sprk_dedupekey. A column would be new surface with no failure mode to cite (root CLAUDE.md section 11).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: no column is added to any table outside the five ontology tables (sprk_triagecategory recall columns are reconciliation C-16, undecided).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: any test written against these columns later must be paired with something touching the real schema; this task's live describe is that evidence.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Dataverse schema creation</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/skills/dataverse-create-schema/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-002-thin-plugins.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/schema-draft.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/001-schema-verification.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/spec.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Column add via Web API" location="projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/001-schema-verification.md">Task 001 added four columns with the recipe; copy its request shape, headers and the live-describe verification.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare the rigor level and reason per root CLAUDE.md section 8, then load the knowledge files above.</step>
    <step order="1">Describe the four tables live and record which of the columns in the constraints already exist (none is expected). Record sprk_dedupekey's MaxLength and the alternate key state.</step>
    <step order="2">Create the sprk_signal, sprk_policy, sprk_policyversion and sprk_decisionrecord columns one at a time with the recipe; publish after each table.</step>
    <step order="3">Add the Retired statuscode value on sprk_policy's Inactive state.</step>
    <step order="4">Raise sprk_dedupekey MaxLength only if the longest episode-scoped key does not fit; confirm the alternate key is still Active.</step>
    <step order="5">Re-key existing sprk_signal rows to episode 1 and re-read them.</step>
    <step order="6">Describe all four tables again and record every new column's logical name, type, length or behaviour in notes/007-schema-verification.md; update notes/schema-draft.md (including the S-7 line: sprk_inforceto IS written at publish, per D-14).</step>
    <step order="7">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task to the completed marker, AND set this POML status element to completed. Both, or scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1 fails the next push.</step>
    <step order="8">Record any deviation from this POML in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any column would land under a prefix other than sprk, or in a solution other than OntologyPlatformSolution, STOP before creating it: logical names are immutable.</trigger>
    <trigger>If raising sprk_dedupekey's MaxLength would require dropping or recreating the alternate key, STOP and escalate rather than recreating it.</trigger>
    <trigger>If either sprk_matter column is SystemRequired (cannot be relaxed through metadata), STOP and escalate: D-35 cannot be implemented by a required-level change.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>The five tables exist (task 001). sprk_policyversion.sprk_proposedaction is a single NVARCHAR(400) slug; sprk_decisionrecord has sprk_actioncode and sprk_action but no step list; sprk_signal has sprk_factsnapshot but no due date; sprk_policy has sprk_name and sprk_enabled but no short name, work type or retired reason (live describe, notes/v4-prototype-vs-solution.md #6, #7).</existing>
    <extension>No for each column: a single-slug proposedaction cannot hold an ordered multi-action plan, and the append-only record cannot be amended later to add steps (#23). The dedupe key is extended in place rather than replaced.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the episode suffix a dismissed or superseded Signal can never re-raise (D-13). Without sprk_duedate the Do-lane re-raise rule has nothing to compare and the row cannot show its due state. Without sprk_steps/sprk_followons the commit route cannot write the one record D-17 requires. Without sprk_decisionplan, Revise budget and Approve variance cannot both be offered by Path B.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="pwsh">Web API calls per the recipe</tool>
    <tool name="dataverse-mcp">Read-only describe and query for verification</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="data">Dataverse: the columns listed under constraints, in OntologyPlatformSolution</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/007-schema-verification.md</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/schema-draft.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a live describe, when read, then every column named in the constraints exists with prefix sprk, in OntologyPlatformSolution, with the stated type; sprk_signal.sprk_duedate has DateTimeBehavior DateOnly.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given sprk_policy, when its status reason is described, then Retired is a value on the Inactive state.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the longest possible episode-scoped key, when compared with sprk_dedupekey's MaxLength, then it fits, and the sprk_dedupekey alternate key is Active.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given every existing sprk_signal row, when read, then its sprk_dedupekey ends in |1 (or the recorded count is zero).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no sprk_episode column exists; no column was added to any table outside sprk_signal, sprk_policy, sprk_policyversion and sprk_decisionrecord; no core-record type column or work-assignment / service-request grouping lookup was added.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given sprk_policy.sprk_severity, when described, then it exists with exactly the Info / Warning / Critical values sprk_signal.sprk_severity uses (D-30).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given sprk_signal.sprk_matter and sprk_decisionrecord.sprk_matter, when described, then their RequiredLevel before and after is recorded in the notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">notes/007-schema-verification.md carries the before and after describes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given sprk_signal and sprk_decisionrecord, when described, then each has an optional sprk_project lookup to sprk_project, and neither has a core-record type column (D-34).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given sprk_signal.sprk_matter and sprk_decisionrecord.sprk_matter, when described, then neither is ApplicationRequired, with the before value recorded (D-35).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec.md FR-03 (amended, D-13), FR-48..FR-51, FR-57; D-30 (severity, decided), D-34 (sprk_project core-record lookup), D-35 (core-record columns optional for no-core-record items). Task 002's union check is repeated by task 008 after these adds (a column add touches the tables the append-only guarantee protects).</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
